CAT = "s24Conduct"; SEG = "CON"
Q = [
("Since March 30, 2026, FINRA Rule 3220 limits gifts given in relation to the business of another person's employer to how much per person per year?",
 '$300', ['$100', '$250', '$500'],
 'FINRA amended Rule 3220 (Regulatory Notice 26-05), effective March 30, 2026, raising the annual limit from $100 to $300 per person. Other rules or firm policies may still set lower limits.'),
("A representative gives a client's employee two concert tickets and does not go to the concert. Under Rule 3220 the tickets are treated as:",
 'A gift that counts toward the annual limit', ['Business entertainment that is not limited', 'A promotional item of nominal value only', 'Non-cash compensation that needs FINRA approval'],
 "Entertainment counts as business entertainment only when the associated person attends. Tickets handed over without the representative present are a gift subject to Rule 3220's annual limit."),
('A representative falsifies an expense report to get reimbursed for personal meals. FINRA can discipline him under Rule 2010:',
 'Even though no securities transaction was involved', ['Only if a customer lost money as a result', 'Only if the amount is over $10,000', 'Never, since expense reports are internal matters'],
 'Rule 2010 requires high standards of commercial honor and just and equitable principles of trade. FINRA has long applied it to unethical business conduct such as falsifying records or converting firm funds, whether or not a security is involved.'),
("A representative wants to borrow $5,000 from his brother, who also has an account with him. Under Rule 3240 the firm:",
 'Need not require notice or approval, though it may', ['Must forbid the loan, since the brother is a customer', 'Must file the loan agreement with FINRA first', 'Must approve it only if the loan carries interest'],
 "Rule 3240 lets a registered person borrow from a customer who is an immediate family member if the firm's procedures allow it. Notice and written approval are required for loans based on personal or business relationships, but the firm is not required to demand them for immediate family, though its procedures may."),
('A registered representative gives the firm written notice of a paid outside business activity under Rule 3270. The firm must:',
 'Assess whether it could interfere or look like firm business', ['Forward the notice to FINRA within 30 days', 'Approve it automatically if it is unpaid work', "Add the activity to the firm's own revenue"],
 "Rule 3270.01 requires the member, on receiving notice, to consider whether the activity will interfere with the person's duties or be viewed by customers as part of the member's business, to decide whether to impose conditions or limits, and to keep a record of its compliance."),
('A representative will receive selling compensation for an outside private securities transaction. Once the firm approves it in writing, the firm must:',
 'Record it on its books and supervise it as its own', ["Only keep a copy of the representative's written notice", 'File the offering documents with the SEC itself', "Report it on the representative's Form U4 as an OBA"],
 "Under Rule 3280 (and Rule 3290 from October 25, 2027), an approved private securities transaction with selling compensation must be recorded on the member's books and supervised as if the member executed it."),
('Under Rule 2040(c), a firm may pay transaction-based compensation to an unregistered foreign finder only if:',
 'The finder and the customers are non-U.S. persons living abroad', ['The finder holds a securities license in some U.S. state', 'The customers are U.S. citizens who live outside the U.S.', 'The finder refers no more than ten customers each year'],
 'Rule 2040(c) allows finder payments to a nonregistered foreign finder when the firm determines the finder need not register as a U.S. broker-dealer, the finder is a non-U.S. citizen or foreign entity domiciled abroad, and the customers are non-U.S. citizens or foreign entities domiciled abroad, among other conditions.'),
("A firm pays a foreign finder under Rule 2040(c). Each confirmation sent to a customer the finder referred must:",
 "State that a referral or finder's fee is paid under an agreement", ["Show the finder's home address and phone number", "Carry the finder's signature as approval of the trade", 'List every other customer the same finder referred'],
 "Rule 2040(c) requires customers to get a document disclosing the finder's compensation and to acknowledge the arrangement in writing, the payments to be recorded on the firm's books, and each confirmation to state that a referral or finder's fee is being paid under an agreement."),
("Under Rule 3160, when a broker-dealer conducts business on a bank's premises, where practical it must:",
 'Work in an area apart from where the bank takes deposits', ["Share the bank's teller windows and its signs", "Hire only the bank's own employees as its representatives", "Have customers sign the bank's deposit account forms"],
 'Rule 3160 requires the member, wherever practical, to conduct its broker-dealer services in a physical location distinct from the area where the financial institution takes retail deposits, with clear signs.'),
("A fund sponsor invites representatives to a training meeting. Under FINRA's non-cash compensation rules the firm may let them attend if:",
 'Attendance is not tied to meeting sales targets', ["The sponsor also pays for each guest's travel", 'Only the top producers are invited to attend it', 'The meeting is held at a beach resort for a week'],
 "Rules 2320 and 2341 allow payment of expenses for training or education meetings only if the member approves, attendance is not conditioned on sales, expenses are not paid for guests and the location suits the meeting's purpose."),
("Under Rule 2150, a representative may share in the profits and losses of a customer's account only if the firm and the customer give prior written approval and the share is:",
 'In proportion to his own contribution', ["At least half of all the account's gains", 'Capped at 10% of the yearly profits', 'Approved by FINRA in advance'],
 "Rule 2150(c) allows sharing in a customer account with prior written authorization from the member and the customer, generally in proportion to the person's financial contribution; accounts jointly held with immediate family are excepted from the proportion test."),
('A representative tells a nervous customer that he will cover any loss on a recommended stock. Under Rule 2150 this is:',
 'A prohibited guarantee against loss', ['Allowed if the promise is put in writing first', 'Allowed for accounts under $10,000', 'Allowed if the firm approves it in writing'],
 'Rule 2150(b) prohibits guaranteeing a customer against loss in connection with any securities transaction or account.'),
("Under Regulation Best Interest's conflict of interest obligation, a broker-dealer must identify and eliminate:",
 'Sales contests tied to specific securities in a limited time', ['All commissions paid on any recommended trades', "Every difference in pay among the firm's various product types", 'Any fee charged to retail customers for advice'],
 'Reg BI requires policies to identify and eliminate sales contests, quotas, bonuses and non-cash compensation based on the sale of specific securities or types of securities within a limited period. Other conflicts may be disclosed or mitigated.'),
('A customer who is not a relative names her registered representative executor of her estate. Under Rule 3241 the representative must:',
 'Notify the firm in writing and get its approval', ['Decline the role unless FINRA approves it first', 'Refuse, since it is always prohibited', 'Tell only the branch manager orally'],
 "Rule 3241 requires a registered person to give prior written notice to the member before being named a customer's beneficiary or holding a position of trust, such as executor, unless the customer is an immediate family member; the firm then approves or rejects it."),
("Under Rule 2060, a firm acting as transfer agent for an issuer that uses the holder lists to solicit trades in that issuer's securities:",
 'May do so only if the issuer requests it', ['May do so at any time, for any customer', 'Must first file the holder list with FINRA', 'May use it only for its institutional clients'],
 'Rule 2060 bars a member that received information as a fiduciary, such as paying or transfer agent, from using it to solicit purchases, sales or exchanges, except at the request and for the benefit of the person that gave the information.'),
("Rule 3290, which replaces Rules 3270 and 3280 on October 25, 2027, requires a registered person's outside activities to be handled by:",
 'Prior written notice; the firm may set conditions or prohibit them', ['Prior approval of each activity by FINRA', 'Annual reporting of all outside activities on Form U4 only', 'A complete ban on all outside business activities by any registered person'],
 "Regulatory Notice 26-20 explains that under Rule 3290 registered persons give prior written notice of outside activities; the member may impose conditions or prohibit them. Outside securities transactions with selling compensation still need the firm's prior written approval."),
]
